\u0bc6\\u0ba9\\u0bcd\\u0ba9\\u0bc8 \\u0baa\\u0bc6\\u0bb0\\u0bc1\\u0ba8\\u0b95\\u0bb0\\u0bae\\u0bbe\\u0b95 \\u0bb5\\u0bb3\\u0bae\\u0bcd \\u0baa\\u0bc6\\u0bb1\\u0bcd\\u0bb1\\u0bc1, \\u0b87\\u0ba9\\u0bcd\\u0bb1\\u0bc1 \\u0b95\\u0bcb\\u0b9f\\u0bbf\\u0b95\\u0bcd\\u0b95\\u0ba3\\u0b95\\u0bcd\\u0b95\\u0bbe\\u0ba9\\u0bb5\\u0bb0\\u0bcd\\u0b95\\u0bb3\\u0bbf\\u0ba9\\u0bcd \\u0bb5\\u0bbe\\u0bb4\\u0bcd\\u0b95\\u0bcd\\u0b95\\u0bc8\\u0b95\\u0bcd \\u0b95\\u0ba9\\u0bb5\\u0bbe\\u0b95 \\u0bb5\\u0bbf\\u0bb0\\u0bbf\\u0ba8\\u0bcd\\u0ba4\\u0bc1 \\u0b95\\u0bbf\\u0b9f\\u0b95\\u0bcd\\u0b95\\u0bbf\\u0bb1\\u0ba4\\u0bc1.\\n\\n\\u0b92\\u0bb1\\u0bcd\\u0bb1\\u0bc1\\u0bae\\u0bc8\\u0b95\\u0bcd\\u0b95\\u0bc1\\u0bae\\u0bcd \\u0b92\\u0ba9\\u0bcd\\u0bb1\\u0bc1\\u0baa\\u0b9f\\u0bcd\\u0b9f \\u0bb5\\u0bb3\\u0bb0\\u0bcd\\u0b9a\\u0bcd\\u0b9a\\u0bbf\\u0b95\\u0bcd\\u0b95\\u0bc1\\u0bae\\u0bcd \\u0b85\\u0b9f\\u0bc8\\u0baf\\u0bbe\\u0bb3\\u0bae\\u0bbe\\u0b95 \\u0ba4\\u0bbf\\u0b95\\u0bb4\\u0bc1\\u0bae\\u0bcd \\u0ba8\\u0bae\\u0bcd \\u0b9a\\u0bc6\\u0ba9\\u0bcd\\u0ba9\\u0bc8\\u0baf\\u0bbf\\u0ba9\\u0bcd \\u0baa\\u0ba9\\u0bcd\\u0bae\\u0bc8\\u0ba4\\u0bcd\\u0ba4\\u0bc1\\u0bb5\\u0ba4\\u0bcd\\u0ba4\\u0bc8 \\u0baa\\u0bbe\\u0ba4\\u0bc1\\u0b95\\u0bbe\\u0ba4\\u0bcd\\u0ba4\\u0bbf\\u0b9f\\u0bc1\\u0bb5\\u0bcb\\u0bae\\u0bcd. \\n\\u0b9a\\u0bc6\\u0ba9\\u0bcd\\u0ba9\\u0bc8 \\u0ba8\\u0bbe\\u0bb3\\u0bcd \\u0bb5\\u0bbe\\u0bb4\\u0bcd\\u0ba4\\u0bcd\\u0ba4\\u0bc1\\u0b95\\u0bb3\\u0bcd!", "Amidst the global trade challenges impacting the textile sector, Honourable Chief Minister of Tamil Nadu Thiru. MK Stalin avargal today met representatives of the textile industry at the Secretariat.", "The delegation expressed their gratitude to the government for the timely grant support extended to set up new processing units with Individual Effluent Treatment Plants (IETP), as well as for the expansion and modernisation of existing dyeing units. These measures not only protect the environment but also safeguard the competitiveness of #Tiruppur\\u2019s globally renowned textile sector.", "Honourable Chief Minister also assured that the state will continue to stand firmly with the sector, working to protect jobs and sustain growth in one of Tamil Nadu\\u2019s most vital industries. We also hope that the Union Government will do its part to shield this crucial export-driven sector from the shocks of global trade disruptions.\\n\\n#InvestInTN", "Our efforts to ensure grounding of MoUs we signed at #TNRising Thoothukudi are on full swing ! \\n\\nHonourable Chief Minister of Tamil Nadu Thiru. MK Stalin avargal today met senior executives of South Korea\\u2019s Hwaseung Footwear Group at the Secretariat.", "Hwaseung has committed an investment of Rs. 1,720 crore to establish a large-scale non-leather footwear manufacturing facility, their first production base in India. This project will generate nearly 20,000 direct jobs, making it one of the largest employment-generating footwear projects in TN. \\n\\nMany more MoUs will soon be converted to #JobsForTN !\\n\\n#InvestInTN #BullishOnTN #DravidianModel", "It was a pleasure to address the centenary celebrations of Good Shepherd Convent & Matriculation Higher Secondary School, Chennai \\u2014 an institution that has shaped generations by imparting education and values.\\n\\nI underlined how Tamil Nadu\\u2019s long tradition of progressive reforms, strengthened by the contributions of Christian & missionary institutions, has enabled girls to excel in all spheres of life.", "As IT Minister, I also urged for a reimagining of existing curricula to attune it towards an AI-driven future, with strong emphasis on human oversight and ethics. Good Shepherd\\u2019s holistic approach and the success of their alumni exemplify their commitment to inclusivity and excellence; the institution\'s legacy will inspire several generations.", "\\u2728Highlights from the Department of Information Technology & Digital Services: Post #24\\n\\nTNeGA_Official: TAMIL NADU ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE MISSIO